            <ArticleTitle>Intracranial tumours presenting with facial pain.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>80-3</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Facial pain is a common presenting symptom in oral surgery outpatient clinics. Among the large number of patients presenting in this way, a small number of patients will be found to have intracranial tumours. Three such cases are described and recommendations made regarding the selection of facial pain patients for further investigation.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
